---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const emailSubject = "mailto:olga@okad.agency?subject=Branded%20Content%20Ads%20%E2%80%94%20tell%20us%20about%20your%20brand";
const calHref = "https://calendly.com/okad_calls/first";
---

<Layout
  title="Branded Content Ads — The Complete Guide to Creator-Powered Advertising | OKAD"
  description="Branded content ads use real creator content as paid advertising across TikTok, Meta, and YouTube. This guide covers delivery methods, creator selection, legal requirements, measurement, and how to run branded content at scale."
>
  <Header />
  <main>

    <!-- Hero -->
    <section class="pt-20 md:pt-24 pb-10 text-center bg-bg">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-accent bg-[rgba(99,102,241,.06)] border border-[rgba(99,102,241,.18)] rounded-full px-3.5 py-1.5 mb-6">
          Open reference &middot; September 2026
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(28px,5vw,48px)] leading-[1.1] tracking-[-0.03em] text-ink mb-4">
          Branded Content Ads: <span class="text-accent">The Complete Guide</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-[18px] text-ink-2 max-w-[600px] mx-auto leading-[1.6] mb-8">
          Branded content ads are paid promotions powered by real creator content. They combine the trust of authentic creator voices with the targeting power of paid media. This guide covers every platform, delivery method, and operational detail.
        </p>
        <div class="flex gap-3 justify-center flex-wrap mb-8">
          <a href={emailSubject} class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-accent text-white hover:bg-accent-hover transition-all no-underline">Order branded content ads &rarr;</a>
          <a href={calHref} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-6 py-3 rounded-xl font-sans text-[14px] font-semibold bg-card text-ink border border-border hover:border-accent hover:text-accent transition-all no-underline">Book a call &rarr;</a>
        </div>
        <div class="flex gap-5 flex-wrap justify-center font-mono text-[12px] text-muted">
          <span>Cross-platform</span>
          <span>Creator-powered</span>
          <span>Authentic feel</span>
          <span>TikTok &middot; Meta &middot; YouTube</span>
          <span>Full-funnel</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- How it works grid -->
    <section class="py-8">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <h2 class="font-display text-[22px] font-bold tracking-[-0.02em] text-center mb-5">How Branded Content Ads Work</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3.5">
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F3AC;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Creator Produces Content</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">A real person films authentic content featuring your product, following a brief that balances brand messaging with creative freedom.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F91D;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Partnership Is Disclosed</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">The content carries a "Paid Partnership" or "Sponsored" label. Transparent, compliant, and built into the platform.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-[10px] p-4 text-center">
            <div class="text-[22px] mb-1.5">&#x1F4B0;</div>
            <h3 class="font-display text-[14px] font-semibold mb-1">Brand Amplifies as Ad</h3>
            <p class="text-[12px] text-muted leading-[1.4]">The creator content is promoted as a paid ad via Spark Ads, Partnership Ads, or whitelabel &mdash; reaching targeted audiences at scale.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- TOC -->
    <section class="py-10 border-t border-b border-border">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-muted-2 mb-4">Contents</div>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-1.5">
          {[
            { num: "01", text: "Overview", href: "#overview" },
            { num: "02", text: "What Makes Content \"Branded\"", href: "#branded" },
            { num: "03", text: "Three Delivery Methods", href: "#delivery" },
            { num: "04", text: "Why Branded Content Outperforms", href: "#performance" },
            { num: "05", text: "Cross-Platform Comparison", href: "#platforms" },
            { num: "06", text: "Creator Selection Criteria", href: "#creators" },
            { num: "07", text: "Brief Structure", href: "#brief" },
            { num: "08", text: "Legal Requirements", href: "#legal" },
            { num: "09", text: "Measurement and ROI", href: "#measurement" },
            { num: "10", text: "OKAD's Branded Content Service", href: "#okad-service" },
            { num: "11", text: "Glossary", href: "#glossary" },
            { num: "12", text: "FAQ", href: "#faq" },
          ].map((item) => (
            <a href={item.href} class="flex items-center gap-2.5 px-3 py-2 rounded-lg text-[14px] text-ink-2 font-medium hover:bg-bg-alt transition-colors no-underline">
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium text-accent min-w-[22px]">{item.num}</span>
              {item.text}
            </a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 01 Overview -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="overview">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">01 &mdash; Overview</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What branded content ads are and why they matter</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Branded content ads = paid promotions powered by creator-made content</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Umbrella term covering Spark Ads, Partnership Ads, and creator-powered YouTube ads</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Content feels authentic because it is &mdash; made by real people, not brand studios</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">"Branded content ads" is the umbrella term for any paid advertisement that uses content created by a real person &mdash; a creator, influencer, or micro-influencer &mdash; rather than content produced entirely by the brand's in-house team or agency. The creator films, edits, and often publishes the content. The brand then amplifies it as a paid ad, leveraging the creator's authentic voice while applying the targeting and scale of paid media.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Each major platform has its own branded content ad format. TikTok calls them <a href="/spark-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Spark Ads</a>. Meta calls them <a href="/partnership-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Partnership Ads</a> (formerly Branded Content Ads). YouTube has BrandConnect and creator-powered video ads. Despite the different names, the underlying mechanic is the same: take content made by a real person and run it as a paid promotion.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">The reason branded content ads have become the dominant format in performance marketing is straightforward: they outperform traditional brand-produced ads. Across industries, branded content ads consistently deliver higher click-through rates, lower cost per acquisition, and stronger engagement than polished studio creatives. The "Paid Partnership" label is visible, but the content itself feels native to the platform &mdash; because it was made by someone who lives on that platform.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This guide covers the complete landscape: what makes content "branded," the three delivery methods, platform-by-platform mechanics, creator selection, briefing, legal requirements, measurement, and how to run branded content ads at scale. For related reading, see our guides on <a href="/guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">creative testing</a>, <a href="/canvas-ugc" class="text-accent hover:underline">Canvas UGC</a>, and <a href="/tech-ugc" class="text-accent hover:underline">Tech UGC</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 02 What Makes Content "Branded" -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="branded">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">02 &mdash; Definition</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">What makes content "branded content"</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Created by a real person, not a brand's internal production team</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Carries a "Paid Partnership" or "Sponsored" label for transparency</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Feels native to the platform despite being a paid promotion</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Branded content sits at the intersection of creator authenticity and brand messaging. The content is produced by a creator who has a genuine voice, visual style, and audience relationship. The brand provides direction &mdash; product information, key messages, tone guidelines &mdash; but the creator retains enough creative freedom that the final piece feels like their own content, not a scripted commercial.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Every major platform requires disclosure when content is the result of a commercial relationship. On TikTok, the "Paid Partnership" toggle labels the post. On Instagram and Facebook, the "Paid partnership with [brand]" header appears above the content. On YouTube, the "Includes paid promotion" disclosure is mandatory. These labels satisfy both platform policy and regulatory requirements (FTC, ASA, and equivalents in other jurisdictions).</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Branded content vs. traditional ads</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Traditional ads are conceived, scripted, filmed, and edited entirely by the brand or its agency. They look like ads. Branded content is conceived collaboratively, produced by a creator, and published in a format native to the platform. The production quality is deliberately "real" rather than polished &mdash; shot on a phone, natural lighting, casual delivery. This is not a weakness; it is the entire point. Platform users have been trained to scroll past anything that looks like an ad. Branded content survives that filter because it looks like content.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The authenticity spectrum</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Not all branded content is equally authentic. At one end, a creator receives a product, uses it genuinely, and shares their honest opinion with minimal brand direction. At the other end, a creator reads a word-for-word script provided by the brand. Both qualify as "branded content," but they perform very differently. The most effective branded content falls in the middle: the brand provides a clear brief with key messages and product facts, but the creator translates those into their own words, shooting style, and storytelling format.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Over-scripted branded content defeats the purpose. If the creator sounds like they are reading a press release, the audience notices immediately. Under-briefed content risks missing the brand's core message or violating compliance requirements. The brief is the lever that determines where content lands on this spectrum &mdash; see <a href="#brief">Section 07</a> for how to structure it.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 03 Three Delivery Methods -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="delivery">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">03 &mdash; Delivery Methods</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Three ways to deliver branded content ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Whitelisting: brand runs ads from the creator's account</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Branded content (tagged): creator posts, brand promotes the post</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Whitelabel: creator delivers footage, brand runs ads from its own account</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Once a creator produces content for a brand, there are three distinct ways that content can be delivered as a paid ad. Each method differs in whose account the ad runs from, what permissions are required, and how the ad appears to the audience. Understanding these three methods is essential for choosing the right approach for your campaign.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Method 1: Whitelisting (creator account access)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">In whitelisting, the creator grants the brand permission to run paid ads directly from the creator's account. The ad appears in the feed as if it were posted by the creator, which maximizes authenticity. On Meta, this is done through Business Manager partnerships. On TikTok, the creator generates an authorization code for <a href="/spark-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Spark Ads</a>. The creator's profile picture, name, and handle appear on the ad. All engagement (likes, comments, shares) accrues to the creator's post.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Whitelisting delivers the strongest native feel but requires the most creator cooperation. Some creators are uncomfortable granting ad account access, especially if they have limited experience with brand partnerships. Clear contracts and transparent communication about how the content will be used are essential.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Method 2: Branded content (tagged promotion)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">In this method, the creator publishes the content on their own account and tags the brand as a paid partner. The brand can then promote this tagged post as a paid ad through its own ad account. On Meta, this is the <a href="/partnership-ads" class="text-accent hover:underline">Partnership Ads</a> format. The post shows the creator's identity but includes the "Paid partnership with [brand]" label. The brand controls targeting, budget, and optimization.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">This method is the most common for branded content ads because it balances authenticity with brand control. The creator publishes organically, the content appears native, and the brand can promote the best-performing posts with paid budget. It requires less account access than whitelisting while preserving the creator's identity in the ad.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Method 3: Whitelabel (brand runs creator footage)</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">In whitelabel delivery, the creator produces content and delivers raw footage to the brand. The brand then publishes and promotes the content from its own account. The creator's identity does not appear on the ad &mdash; the brand's account is the publisher. This gives the brand full control over editing, posting schedule, and ad optimization, but sacrifices the social proof of having a real creator's name and profile attached to the ad.</p>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Whitelabel is common in performance marketing campaigns where the brand needs maximum creative control and plans to test many variations of the same footage. It is also used when creators prefer not to have their profile associated with paid ads or when the brand wants to run the content across multiple platforms simultaneously.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Aspect</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Whitelisting</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Branded Content (Tagged)</th>
                <th class="font-display font-semibold text-[13px] px-4 py-3 text-left border-b border-border">Whitelabel</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Ad runs from</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator's account</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator's post, promoted by brand</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brand's account</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Creator identity visible</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Yes &mdash; full profile</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Yes &mdash; with "Paid Partnership" label</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">No &mdash; brand only</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Authenticity level</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Highest</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">High</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Moderate</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Brand control</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Limited (targeting only)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Moderate (targeting + budget)</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Full (edit, post, optimize)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Creator permission needed</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Account access</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brand tag approval</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Usage rights only</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink">Engagement accrues to</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator's post</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Creator's post</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 border-b border-border text-ink-2">Brand's post</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink">Best for</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Max authenticity, social proof</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Balanced approach, most campaigns</td><td class="px-4 py-2.5 text-ink-2">Performance testing, full control</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Most brands use a combination of all three methods depending on the campaign objective, creator relationship, and platform. OKAD typically recommends starting with branded content (tagged) for initial campaigns and layering in whitelisting for top-performing creators who are comfortable with deeper partnerships.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 04 Why Branded Content Outperforms -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="performance">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">04 &mdash; Performance</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Why branded content outperforms traditional ads</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Trust: people trust people more than brands</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Native feel: content survives the "scroll past ads" reflex</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Algorithm preference: platforms reward engagement, and branded content gets more of it</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Branded content ads outperform traditional studio-produced ads for reasons that are structural, not accidental. The advantages compound: each factor reinforces the others to create a meaningful performance gap.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Trust and credibility</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Audiences have developed sophisticated instincts for detecting advertisements. A polished, brand-produced video triggers an immediate "this is an ad" response, activating skepticism. Branded content bypasses this filter because it is delivered by a real person whose content style matches what the viewer already consumes. The message is the same &mdash; "this product is good" &mdash; but the messenger is trusted. Studies consistently show that consumers trust recommendations from individuals over brand messaging, even when they know the individual is being compensated.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Native format and platform fit</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Branded content is produced in the same format, aspect ratio, editing style, and pacing that performs natively on each platform. A TikTok branded content ad looks like a TikTok. An Instagram Reel branded content ad looks like a Reel. This is not cosmetic &mdash; platform algorithms prioritize content that keeps users on the platform, and native-feeling content achieves higher watch time, completion rates, and engagement than content that disrupts the feed experience.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Social proof</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">When a branded content ad runs from a creator's account (via whitelisting or tagged promotion), it inherits the creator's social context: their followers, their content history, their engagement patterns. A viewer can tap the creator's profile and see a real person with real content. This social proof is impossible to replicate with brand-account ads. It transforms the ad from an anonymous promotion into a personal recommendation.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Algorithm preference</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Platform algorithms optimize for engagement. Branded content consistently generates more likes, comments, shares, and saves than traditional ad creatives because it feels like organic content. Higher engagement signals tell the algorithm to show the content to more people, creating a positive feedback loop. On TikTok, Spark Ads that use existing high-performing organic posts benefit from accumulated engagement signals, often achieving 30&ndash;50% lower CPMs compared to standard in-feed ads.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Creative diversity at scale</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Working with multiple creators produces natural creative variation. Each creator brings their own voice, delivery style, hooks, and visual approach. This diversity is extremely difficult to replicate internally. A brand working with 10 creators gets 10 distinct perspectives on the same product, which feeds the <a href="/guide" class="text-accent hover:underline">creative testing</a> process with diverse hypotheses. In traditional production, generating this level of variation requires deliberate scripting and multiple production days.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- 05 Cross-Platform Comparison -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="platforms">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">05 &mdash; Platforms</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">Cross-platform comparison</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">TikTok: Spark Ads &mdash; strongest native ad format, highest organic discovery</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Meta: Partnership Ads &mdash; most mature targeting, largest audience</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">YouTube: BrandConnect &amp; creator ads &mdash; longest watch time, strongest for consideration</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Each platform implements branded content ads differently. The format names, setup workflows, permission structures, and performance characteristics vary significantly. This comparison covers the three major platforms for branded content advertising as of 2026.</p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-border bg-card mb-6">
          <table class="w-full border-collapse text-[14px]">
            <thead class="bg-bg">
              <tr>
