    <!-- 06 Creator Selection Criteria -->
    <section class="guide-section" id="creators">
      <div class="max-w-[800px] mx-auto px-6">
        <div class="font-mono text-[11px] font-medium uppercase tracking-[.1em] text-accent mb-2">06 &mdash; Creator Selection</div>
        <h2 class="font-display font-bold text-[clamp(24px,3.5vw,32px)] leading-[1.15] tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink mb-2">How to select the right creators</h2>
        <div class="tldr">
          <ul class="list-none p-0 m-0 space-y-1">
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Niche fit matters more than follower count</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Evaluate content quality, audience demographics, and engagement rate</li>
            <li class="text-[14px] text-ink-2 before:content-['—_'] before:text-accent before:font-semibold">Vet creators for brand safety and compliance history</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">Creator selection is the single most important variable in branded content performance. The wrong creator produces content that feels forced, misses the target audience, or fails to communicate the brand's value proposition. The right creator makes it look effortless &mdash; because for them, it nearly is. They already create content in the brand's niche, their audience matches the brand's target customer, and their production quality meets the bar for paid media.</p>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">The five selection criteria</h3>
        <ol class="list-none p-0 counter-reset-step space-y-0">
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Niche fit.</strong> The creator's existing content should naturally overlap with the brand's product category. A fitness creator reviewing a protein supplement is believable. A gaming creator reviewing the same supplement is not &mdash; unless their audience is gym-going gamers. Look at the creator's last 30 posts, not just their bio.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Content quality.</strong> Evaluate production value (lighting, audio, framing), storytelling ability (hooks, pacing, payoff), and platform fluency (trends, editing techniques, format awareness). A creator does not need professional equipment, but they do need to produce content that holds attention for the full duration.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Audience demographics.</strong> Request audience data or use third-party analytics tools. Key metrics: age distribution, gender split, geographic concentration, and interests. A creator with 500K followers is worthless for your campaign if 80% of their audience is in a country you do not serve.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative border-b border-border text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Engagement rate.</strong> Calculate engagement rate as (likes + comments) / followers or views. Industry benchmarks vary by platform: TikTok 3&ndash;8%, Instagram 1&ndash;4%, YouTube 2&ndash;6%. A high engagement rate signals an active, responsive audience. Low engagement relative to follower count often indicates purchased followers or an inactive audience.</li>
          <li class="py-3.5 pl-[52px] relative text-ink-2 guide-step"><strong>Brand safety and compliance.</strong> Review the creator's content history for controversial statements, competitor partnerships, compliance violations, and overall tone alignment with the brand. Check whether the creator has experience with disclosure requirements (FTC, platform labels). A creator who has never done a brand deal may need additional guidance on compliance.</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="font-display font-semibold text-[20px] tracking-[-0.01em] mt-8 mb-3">Micro-creators vs. macro-creators</h3>
        <p class="text-ink-2 leading-[1.65] mb-4">For branded content ads, micro-creators (10K&ndash;100K followers) often outperform macro-creators (500K+). Micro-creators have higher engagement rates, more niche audiences, lower rates, and greater willingness to follow briefs closely. They also produce content that feels more authentic &mdash; a recommendation from someone with 25K followers reads differently than one from a celebrity. The optimal strategy for most brands is working with 5&ndash;15 micro-creators simultaneously rather than 1&ndash;2 large influencers.</p>

        <div class="bg-card border border-border rounded-xl p-6 my-6 flex gap-4 items-start flex-col sm:flex-row">
